lisa-design:
NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY=1 in vmrun.Setup's env rather than pre-installing yarn in base.sh: node v24.21.0 bundles corepack 0.36.0, which since 0.35.0 fetches through Node's built-in fetch and honours HTTP(S)_PROXY only behind NODE_USE_ENV_PROXY (Node added it in v24.0.0). One env var fixes yarn and pnpm, any version a repo's packageManager names, and every other Node fetch/http client, with no base rebuild. yarn classic itself (request) and npm (@npmcli/agent) already read HTTPS_PROXY. Accepted trade-off: Node's NO_PROXY has no CIDR, so Node clients reaching a private IP go through the gateway.
